---
description: Lingotran QA house rules — applies to the manual and to any test code
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` at the repo root before editing. They are the source of
truth; this file only points at them so the standard does not fork per tool.

Non-negotiable here:

- Never edit `dist/` — it is generated. Edit `src/`, then `bash scripts/build.sh`.
- `python scripts/verify.py` must pass clean before a change is done.
- SELECT-only against any database, and never a production host.
- No learner audio, learner names, credentials or connection strings in a prompt.
  Learners are minors. Use IDs and correlation IDs.
- Lingotran is the only product discussed. Stack tool names are fine.

Writing Playwright for Lingotran:

- Seed state via the API, never through the UI — the largest source of flake and runtime.
- Locate by `getByRole` with an accessible name, never a CSS class.
- No `waitForTimeout`.
- Assert the database at the end. A green UI over a wrong row is the defect that ships.
- One assertion theme per test.
- Fresh data per test; shared fixtures create order dependence that only shows up in CI.

If a test passes before the feature exists, that is a broken assertion. Say so rather
than reporting success.
